-- ===========================================================================
-- truvio-demo layer - what fills the product detail page
-- ===========================================================================
-- The parity report counted marine's flagship PDP at twenty-one sections and
-- truvio's at eight, four of them empty, with the whole page measuring 84
-- characters of main text. Four of those sections had no DATA to draw, which is
-- what this file supplies: a gallery, a documents table, relations, and a
-- specification table filled to seven of seven rather than three.
--
-- WHAT IT WRITES
--   Gallery. Every master already carries its concept tile as the default
--     image. Each now gains the photographic frame its TOP group is branded
--     with, and two rows in five gain a third detail shot, so the thumbnail
--     strip has something to step through and the card and the page do not
--     always open on the same picture. Two to four images per master, matching
--     the Media Set value the specification table states for the same row.
--     The photographic targets are the Distribution's own brand manifest
--     entries (brand/brand-assets.manifest.json: product-shot-1/2/3,
--     product-visual, ui-composite), fetched at brand time and never committed
--     as binaries - so the paths here are the manifest's `target` values
--     verbatim, and a solution that has not run its brand step shows the tile
--     alone rather than a broken page.
--   Documents. The platform shape is an ASSET CATEGORY, not a product file
--     field: one EcomDetailsGroup named `Manuals` (extensions pdf,
--     InheritanceType 3, ControlType 0) with EcomDetails rows per product,
--     which is what Swift's ProductMediaTable binds to when it is configured
--     ImageAssets=["Manuals"]. The column values are read off a live DW 10
--     solution carrying a working Manuals group rather than guessed, because a
--     NULL ControlType / InheritanceType on that group is a known silent
--     failure: the group exists, the rows exist, and every PDP renders zero
--     links with no error anywhere.
--   Two PDFs per top group, shipped in this layer's own files/ and generated by
--     tools/make-documents.py - a one-page datasheet and a one-page install
--     guide, base-14 Helvetica so nothing is embedded, about a kilobyte each.
--     They are DATA, like the concept tiles: what a row points at, never a
--     style.
--   Relations, in three groups. `Related products` gives every master the other
--     three rows in its own band. `Accessories` gives it the same slot in the
--     two sibling bands under its top group. `Spare parts` carries the kit
--     story BOTH WAYS - a kit relates to its members and each member relates
--     back - because a relation that reads from one end only is half a demo.
--   The remaining four category-field values per master, taking the
--     specification table from three rows to seven on every page.
--
-- Apply after truvio-catalog.sql (which owns the taxonomy and the first three
-- values) and after truvio-images.sql (which owns the default image).
-- Idempotent: every row is guarded on its own key.
-- ===========================================================================
SET NOCOUNT ON;
SET XACT_ABORT ON;
BEGIN TRAN;

IF OBJECT_ID(N'dbo.EcomDetailsGroup', N'U') IS NULL
   OR OBJECT_ID(N'dbo.EcomProductsRelated', N'U') IS NULL
   OR OBJECT_ID(N'dbo.EcomProductsRelatedGroups', N'U') IS NULL
    RAISERROR(N'truvio-pdp.sql: an asset-category or relation table is missing. The documents table and the related-products strip have nothing to bind to on this platform build.', 16, 1);
IF COL_LENGTH('EcomDetails', 'DetailsGroupId') IS NULL
   OR COL_LENGTH('EcomDetailsGroup', 'DetailsGroupControlType') IS NULL
   OR COL_LENGTH('EcomDetailsGroup', 'DetailsGroupInheritanceType') IS NULL
   OR COL_LENGTH('EcomDetailsGroup', 'DetailsGroupExtensions') IS NULL
   OR COL_LENGTH('EcomProductsRelated', 'ProductRelatedProductRelVariantID') IS NULL
    RAISERROR(N'truvio-pdp.sql: the asset-category or relation columns are not the expected shape. Read the live column names off sys.columns and update this file - do NOT let it seed a documents table the PDP cannot resolve.', 16, 1);

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. The gallery.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
